WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:03.760
All right, let's get into audience questions for&nbsp;
the week. First one is about the one point nine&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.760 --> 00:00:09.440
trillion dollar coronavirus stimulus bill. And&nbsp;
there's a bunch of versions of this going around.&nbsp;

00:00:10.480 --> 00:00:14.080
But the question is, why are all&nbsp;
of these right wingers saying&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:19.360
that most of the one point nine dollars trillion&nbsp;
has nothing to do with coronavirus if it's a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.360 --> 00:00:25.280
coronavirus relief bill? Now, this isn't true.&nbsp;
We're going to go through what is in this bill&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.280 --> 00:00:32.080
and actually talk about the origins of this claim&nbsp;
that most of the money isn't for covid stimulus,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.080 --> 00:00:37.440
but this is not a new claim from Republicans.
They did the exact same thing with Hurricane&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.440 --> 00:00:44.320
Sandy, Hurricane Sandy when it hit New York&nbsp;
and New Jersey years ago. I think it was 2012.&nbsp;

00:00:44.320 --> 00:00:52.160
The response bill contained not only money&nbsp;
to fix the damage that happened, but also&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.160 --> 00:00:59.120
because American infrastructure is woefully&nbsp;
outdated and because we haven't elected&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.680 --> 00:01:06.240
a system of elected government that doesn't&nbsp;
incentivize thinking proactively spending now&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.120 --> 00:01:11.360
to prevent a problem in the future&nbsp;
that will cause us to spend more money.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.360 --> 00:01:15.200
We are in the unfortunate situation&nbsp;
where sometimes in order to get things&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.840 --> 00:01:22.000
fixed and prevent future problems, you have to do&nbsp;
it when a system breaks and you have a problem.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.120 --> 00:01:28.800
With Hurricane Sandy, you saw that there was a&nbsp;
bunch of money in the Hurricane Sandy relief bill,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.800 --> 00:01:33.600
which people like Ted Cruz referred to as&nbsp;
pork, and there was some pork, but a lot of it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.600 --> 00:01:40.160
was not that meant to strengthen infrastructure.
When you look at the flooding that took place,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.160 --> 00:01:45.600
when you look at the breakdown of all sorts of&nbsp;
different resources and infrastructure at that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:50.720
time, the idea was, hey, we now have evidence&nbsp;
that because we didn't strengthen this stuff,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.720 --> 00:01:57.840
because it's so not robust, it's so fragile when&nbsp;
we have a situation like a hurricane that hits&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.840 --> 00:02:02.640
an area that less frequently gets hurricanes,&nbsp;
New York and New Jersey, all this stuff breaks.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:08.560
So as part of recovering, let's also strengthen&nbsp;
things for the future. OK, with that framework,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.560 --> 00:02:14.160
the meme that's been going around is, well, hold&nbsp;
on a second. If each American, not everybody,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.160 --> 00:02:18.960
but most Americans get fourteen hundred&nbsp;
bucks and then you get some money for kids,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.960 --> 00:02:24.800
you'll see it floating around that only a few&nbsp;
hundred billion of the one point nine trillion&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.800 --> 00:02:33.280
is for covid. This is so silly. But because it's&nbsp;
being repeated so much, it's worth understanding&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.280 --> 00:02:40.080
that in the one point nine trillion you have, for&nbsp;
example, one hundred and sixty billion for vaccine&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.640 --> 00:02:49.200
purchases, distribution, injection, as well as&nbsp;
covid testing. That's covid related. It's not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.200 --> 00:02:56.160
cash for people, but the more we vaccinate, the&nbsp;
the faster we do away with this pandemic and the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.160 --> 00:03:01.520
more the economy will recover. Come on, guys.&nbsp;
You're saying that's not actually for covid?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.520 --> 00:03:06.240
Three hundred and sixty billion for state and&nbsp;
local governments to make sure that they are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.240 --> 00:03:13.120
solvent, solvent? Many states, because of the&nbsp;
when you have a reduction in business activity,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.760 --> 00:03:20.400
states where those businesses exist&nbsp;
taken reduced tax revenue, the states&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:26.400
still hopefully are providing police, fire,&nbsp;
school, you know, all this different stuff. So&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.960 --> 00:03:31.280
as a result of coronavirus, a bunch of different&nbsp;
states need money. You're really going to say&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:31.280 --> 00:03:38.080
that's not coronavirus related, eight and a&nbsp;
half billion for rural hospitals to stay open.&nbsp;

00:03:38.080 --> 00:03:41.520
And of course, those are going to be&nbsp;
important vaccination sites in rural areas,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.080 --> 00:03:48.400
25 billion to fund child care centers that&nbsp;
you're going to say that has nothing to do with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.400 --> 00:03:53.600
coronavirus. One of the issues we have right&nbsp;
now is many parents can't get back to work.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:54.720 --> 00:04:00.560
If their kids aren't back in school, so you very&nbsp;
quickly start to understand why funding childcare,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:00.560 --> 00:04:05.520
which, by the way, we don't fund enough in this&nbsp;
country anyway, is related to coronavirus 15&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:05.520 --> 00:04:10.480
billion to subsidize child care for essential&nbsp;
workers. We need our essential workers to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:10.480 --> 00:04:16.800
working. They need to be working to make money.&nbsp;
But if they have to be taking care of their kids,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:16.800 --> 00:04:22.080
they can't work and then they can't put food on&nbsp;
their family's table. This is it's coronavirus&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:22.080 --> 00:04:27.440
related. Why are we in this situation, 130 billion&nbsp;
for K through 12 schools to reopen and decrease&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:27.440 --> 00:04:33.280
class sizes. It costs money to decrease class&nbsp;
sizes to open safely. If you decrease class sizes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:33.280 --> 00:04:39.040
you either need additional teachers to have way&nbsp;
more classes or you need to be paying overtime.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:39.040 --> 00:04:42.880
If teachers are going to be doing two sessions,&nbsp;
however you're going to do it, it's going to cost&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:42.880 --> 00:04:48.320
money. People on the right wants schools open.&nbsp;
People on the left want schools open safely.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:48.880 --> 00:04:54.480
Here's money. In order to do that, we could go&nbsp;
on and on and on, you know, 15 billion dollars to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:54.480 --> 00:04:59.440
prevent airline layoffs. OK, there are some who&nbsp;
are saying airlines should be allowed to fail.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:05.600
Unfortunately, er er fortunately or unfortunately,&nbsp;
whatever the case may be, airlines are a big&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:05.600 --> 00:05:09.360
piece of infrastructure, transportation&nbsp;
infrastructure. You could make the case,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:09.360 --> 00:05:16.240
let them fail, but we're going to be depending on&nbsp;
airlines if and when things start to improve, to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:17.680 --> 00:05:22.400
allow commerce and allow travel to restart&nbsp;
travel, one of the hardest hit industries.&nbsp;

00:05:22.400 --> 00:05:28.560
So, you know, you can make a case on any of&nbsp;
these things. Well, maybe the 15 should be 12&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:28.560 --> 00:05:32.720
or something like that. But the&nbsp;
talking point that's floating around&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:32.720 --> 00:05:37.360
is most of the money has nothing to&nbsp;
do with coronavirus. And of course,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:37.360 --> 00:05:42.400
that is completely and totally untrue. This&nbsp;
isn't a new talking point from the right,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:42.960 --> 00:05:47.120
and it's not at all surprising that they're&nbsp;
rehashing it and reviving it right now.

